# CODEOWNERS — review routing per Review-F5 roadmap §2.2.
# Separates data/content ownership (linguists / content team) from NLU code
# ownership (engineering) so data edits and engine edits get the right review.
# NOTE: team handles below are placeholders — replace with real GitHub
# teams/users once the org structure is provisioned (tracked in
# docs/Review-F5/EXECUTION_STATUS.md "Needs decision" queue).

# Default: engineering owns everything not matched below.
*                         @intentclassifier/engineering

# --- Data & content (linguists / content team) ------------------------------
/data/                    @intentclassifier/content
/config/calibration.json  @intentclassifier/ml-engineering
/multilingual/data/       @intentclassifier/content

# --- NLU engine & pipelines (engineering) -----------------------------------
/scripts/nlu/             @intentclassifier/engineering
/scripts/                 @intentclassifier/engineering
/multilingual/            @intentclassifier/ml-engineering

# --- Architecture docs & ADRs -----------------------------------------------
/docs/Review-F5/          @intentclassifier/architecture

# --- CI / repo meta ----------------------------------------------------------
/.github/                 @intentclassifier/engineering
/Makefile                 @intentclassifier/engineering
/pyproject.toml           @intentclassifier/engineering
/requirements*.txt        @intentclassifier/engineering
/requirements.lock        @intentclassifier/engineering
